  "scope": "One ValidatingAdmissionPolicy and ValidatingAdmissionPolicyBinding on two owned Kind API servers. The policy denies Pod CREATE requests setting hostNetwork=true in one case-labeled namespace; ordinary hostNetwork=false Pods remain permitted. Remote drift changes only that binding's validationActions from Deny to Warn. A distinct scoped writer makes the change, a bounded reconciler restores the desired revision, and an independent consumer verifies actual API state. The additive scratch check reintroduces one drift and requires one actual CronJob-owned in-cluster pass plus an independent read of its metadata-only receipt. It does not prove recurring fleet monitoring or external alert delivery. All probe Pods use a nonexistent scheduler name and never run.",
